§§ `Rule 3 -- service on Government`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "Order 7, Order 8 and any other provision of these Rules relating to service out of Singapore do not apply ..."
-- A flat statement about the overridden provisions (S-L2): JUST FALSE that they apply.
-- src:6918 | 3. —(1) Order 7, Order 8 and any other provision of these Rules relating to service out of Singapore do not apply in relation to the service of any process by which civil proceedings against the Government are begun. (2) Personal service of any document required to be served on the Government for the purpose of or in connection with any civil proceedings is not requisite; but where the proceedings are by or against the Government, service on the Government must be effected — ( a )
@ref O 59 r 3(1) (src:6918)
GIVEN `the process is one by which civil proceedings against the Government are begun` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is Order 7, Order 8 or another provision relating to service out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 3(1) the provision applies to the service of the process` MEANS
    IF `the process is one by which civil proceedings against the Government are begun` AND `the provision is Order 7, Order 8 or another provision relating to service out of Singapore`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Order 7, Order 8 and any other provision of these Rules relating to service out of Singapore do not apply in relation to the service of any process by which civil proceedings against the Government are begun"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 3(1) speaks of the service of "any process by which civil proceedings against the Government are begun" and of those provisions only

-- (2): "Personal service of any document required to be served on the Government ... is not requisite".
-- src:6918 | 3. —(1) Order 7, Order 8 and any other provision of these Rules relating to service out of Singapore do not apply in relation to the service of any process by which civil proceedings against the Government are begun. (2) Personal service of any document required to be served on the Government for the purpose of or in connection with any civil proceedings is not requisite; but where the proceedings are by or against the Government, service on the Government must be effected — ( a )
@ref O 59 r 3(2) (src:6918)
GIVEN `the document is required to be served on the Government for the purpose of or in connection with civil proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
