-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 7 -- judgment in default`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 59 r 7(1) kind of default` IS ONE OF
    `o 59 r 7(1) default of notice of intention to contest or not contest`
    `o 59 r 7(1) default of pleading`
    `o 59 r 7(1) another kind of default`

DECLARE `o 59 r 7(1) proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `o 59 r 7(1) civil proceedings against the Government`
    `o 59 r 7(1) third party proceedings against the Government`
    `o 59 r 7(1) other proceedings`

-- (1): "Except with the permission of the Court, no judgment in default ... may be entered against the Government ...".
-- The bar as its own yes/no: JUST TRUE where it bars, JUST FALSE where permission has been given; outside the described
-- default and proceedings the bar is not this Rule's: NOTHING (a scope limit, ruling (c)).
-- src:6949 | 7. —(1) Except with the permission of the Court, no judgment in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or of pleading may be entered against the Government in civil proceedings against the Government or in third party proceedings against the Government. (2) Except with the permission of the Court, Order 10, Rule 5(1)( a ) does not apply in the case of third party proceedings against the Government.
@ref O 59 r 7(1) (src:6949)
GIVEN default IS A `o 59 r 7(1) kind of default`
      proceedings IS A `o 59 r 7(1) proceedings`
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 7(1) judgment in default is barred without permission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF default EQUALS `o 59 r 7(1) another kind of default` OR proceedings EQUALS `o 59 r 7(1) other proceedings`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 7(1) speaks of "judgment in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or of pleading" in "civil proceedings against the Government or in third party proceedings against the Government"
        IF `the Court has given permission`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except with the permission of the Court"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The permission question: QA: once permission is given the bar is lifted and grants nothing: NOTHING / other: JUST TRUE.
-- src:6949 | 7. —(1) Except with the permission of the Court, no judgment in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or of pleading may be entered against the Government in civil proceedings against the Government or in third party proceedings against the Government. (2) Except with the permission of the Court, Order 10, Rule 5(1)( a ) does not apply in the case of third party proceedings against the Government.
@ref O 59 r 7(1) (src:6949)
GIVEN default IS A `o 59 r 7(1) kind of default`
      proceedings IS A `o 59 r 7(1) proceedings`
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 7(1) judgment in default may be entered against the Government` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`o 59 r 7(1) judgment in default is barred without permission` default proceedings `the Court has given permission` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar does not arise on these facts (or permission has lifted it), and a lifted bar grants nothing; QA: NOTHING / other: JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no judgment in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or of pleading may be entered against the Government"

-- (2): "Except with the permission of the Court, Order 10, Rule 5(1)(a) does not apply in the case of third party proceedings
-- against the Government."  A flat statement about O 10 (S-L2); QA once permission is given.
-- src:6949 | 7. —(1) Except with the permission of the Court, no judgment in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or of pleading may be entered against the Government in civil proceedings against the Government or in third party proceedings against the Government. (2) Except with the permission of the Court, Order 10, Rule 5(1)( a ) does not apply in the case of third party proceedings against the Government.
-- src:6950 | (3) An application for permission under this Rule must be made by summons, and the summons must be served at least 14 days before the return day.
@ref O 59 r 7(2) (src:6949-6950)
GIVEN proceedings IS A `o 59 r 7(1) proceedings`
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 7(2) Order 10 rule 5(1)(a) applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF proceedings EQUALS `o 59 r 7(1) third party proceedings against the Government` AND NOT (`the Court has given permission`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply in the case of third party proceedings against the Government"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 7(2) speaks of third party proceedings against the Government, and once the Court gives permission the exception grants nothing; QA: NOTHING / other: JUST TRUE

`o 59 r 7(3) the period for serving the summons before the return day` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

-- src:6950 | (3) An application for permission under this Rule must be made by summons, and the summons must be served at least 14 days before the return day.
@ref O 59 r 7(3) (src:6950)
GIVEN `the application is one for permission under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `Document kind`
      `the date the summons was served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 7(3) the application for permission is made and served as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is one for permission under this Rule`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 7(3) speaks of "An application for permission under this Rule"
        IF `the date the summons was served` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the summons must be served at least 14 days before the return day"
        IF document EQUALS Summons
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be made by summons"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 8 -- third party notice`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "a third party notice ... for service on the Government must not be issued without the permission of the Court" -- a bar
-- with an exception (QA); and the application "must be made by summons, and the summons must be served on the claimant and the Government".
-- src:6952 | 8. —(1) Despite anything in Order 10, a third party notice (including a notice issuable by virtue of Order 10, Rule 9) for service on the Government must not be issued without the permission of the Court, and the application for the grant of such permission must be made by summons, and the summons must be served on the claimant and the Government. (2) Permission to issue such a notice for service on the Government must not be granted unless the Court is satisfied that the Government is in possession of all such information as it reasonably requires as to the circumstances in which it is alleged that the liability of the Government has arisen and as to the departments and officers of the Government concerned.
@ref O 59 r 8(1) (src:6952)
GIVEN `the notice is a third party notice, including one issuable by virtue of Order 10 rule 9, for service on the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 8(1) the third party notice may be issued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the notice is a third party notice, including one issuable by virtue of Order 10 rule 9, for service on the Government`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 8(1) speaks of "a third party notice (including a notice issuable by virtue of Order 10, Rule 9) for service on the Government"
        IF `the Court has given permission`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is lifted by the permission, and a lifted bar grants nothing; QA: NOTHING / other: JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be issued without the permission of the Court"

-- src:6952 | 8. —(1) Despite anything in Order 10, a third party notice (including a notice issuable by virtue of Order 10, Rule 9) for service on the Government must not be issued without the permission of the Court, and the application for the grant of such permission must be made by summons, and the summons must be served on the claimant and the Government. (2) Permission to issue such a notice for service on the Government must not be granted unless the Court is satisfied that the Government is in possession of all such information as it reasonably requires as to the circumstances in which it is alleged that the liability of the Government has arisen and as to the departments and officers of the Government concerned.
@ref O 59 r 8(1) (src:6952)
GIVEN `the application is one for permission to issue such a notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `Document kind`
      `the summons is served on the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons is served on the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 8(1) the application for permission is made and served as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is one for permission to issue such a notice`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 8(1) speaks of "the application for the grant of such permission"
        IF document EQUALS Summons AND `the summons is served on the claimant` AND `the summons is served on the Government`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be made by summons, and the summons must be served on the claimant and the Government"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- (2): "Permission ... must not be granted unless the Court is satisfied that the Government is in possession of all such
-- information as it reasonably requires ...": a bar on the Court with an "unless"; satisfied: QA: NOTHING / other: JUST TRUE.
-- src:6952 | 8. —(1) Despite anything in Order 10, a third party notice (including a notice issuable by virtue of Order 10, Rule 9) for service on the Government must not be issued without the permission of the Court, and the application for the grant of such permission must be made by summons, and the summons must be served on the claimant and the Government. (2) Permission to issue such a notice for service on the Government must not be granted unless the Court is satisfied that the Government is in possession of all such information as it reasonably requires as to the circumstances in which it is alleged that the liability of the Government has arisen and as to the departments and officers of the Government concerned.
