-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 9 -- production`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): an order under section 34(1) "is to be construed as not requiring the disclosure of any document the withholding of which is
-- authorised or required under any other written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest".
-- src:6954 | 9. —(1) In any civil proceedings to which the Government is a party, any order of the Court made under the powers conferred by section 34(1) is to be construed as not requiring the disclosure of any document the withholding of which is authorised or required under any other written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest. (2) Where in any such proceedings an order of the Court directs that a list of documents made in answer to an order for production against the Government must be verified by affidavit, the affidavit must be made by such officer of the Government as the Court may direct.
@ref O 59 r 9(1) (src:6954)
GIVEN `the proceedings are civil proceedings to which the Government is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was made under the powers conferred by section 34(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the withholding of the document is authorised or required under any other written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 9(1) the order requires disclosure of the document` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are civil proceedings to which the Government is a party` AND `the order was made under the powers conferred by section 34(1)` AND `the withholding of the document is authorised or required under any other written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be construed as not requiring the disclosure of any document the withholding of which is authorised or required under any other written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 9(1) construes an order under section 34(1) in respect of a document whose withholding is authorised or required on the public-interest ground, and says nothing of any other order or document

-- src:6954 | 9. —(1) In any civil proceedings to which the Government is a party, any order of the Court made under the powers conferred by section 34(1) is to be construed as not requiring the disclosure of any document the withholding of which is authorised or required under any other written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest. (2) Where in any such proceedings an order of the Court directs that a list of documents made in answer to an order for production against the Government must be verified by affidavit, the affidavit must be made by such officer of the Government as the Court may direct.
@ref O 59 r 9(2) (src:6954)
GIVEN `the proceedings are civil proceedings to which the Government is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order directs that a list of documents made in answer to an order for production against the Government be verified by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit is made by the officer of the Government whom the Court directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 9(2) the affidavit verifying the list is made by the officer the Court directed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proceedings are civil proceedings to which the Government is a party` AND `an order directs that a list of documents made in answer to an order for production against the Government be verified by affidavit`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 9(2) speaks of "such proceedings" and of an order that a list of documents made in answer to an order for production against the Government be verified by affidavit
        IF `the affidavit is made by the officer of the Government whom the Court directed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "the affidavit must be made by such officer of the Government as the Court may direct"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

