§§ `Rule 10 -- evidence`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6956 | 10. To avoid doubt, it is declared that any powers exercisable by the Court in regard to the taking of evidence are exercisable in proceedings by or against the Government as they are exercisable in proceedings between subjects.
@ref O 59 r 10 (src:6956)
GIVEN `the proceedings are by or against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 10 the Court's powers in regard to the taking of evidence are exercisable as between subjects` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are by or against the Government`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 10 declares the powers exercisable "in proceedings by or against the Government" and says nothing of other proceedings

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 11 -- enforcement and satisfaction of orders`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "Nothing in Order 22, Order 23 and Order 13, Rule 9 apply in respect of any order against the Government."  A flat statement about
-- the overridden Orders (S-L2).
-- src:6958 | 11. —(1) Nothing in Order 22, Order 23 and Order 13, Rule 9 apply in respect of any order against the Government. (2) An application under the proviso to section 31(1) for a direction that a separate certificate is to be issued under that subsection with respect to the costs (if any) ordered to be paid to the applicant, may be made to the Court by summons without notice.
@ref O 59 r 11(1) (src:6958)
GIVEN `the order is an order against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      provision IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 11(1) the provision applies in respect of the order` MEANS
    IF `the order is an order against the Government` AND elem provision (LIST
        "Order 22",
        "Order 23",
        "Order 13 rule 9")
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in Order 22, Order 23 and Order 13, Rule 9 apply in respect of any order against the Government"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only Order 22, Order 23 and Order 13 rule 9 are named, and only in respect of an order against the Government

-- src:6958 | 11. —(1) Nothing in Order 22, Order 23 and Order 13, Rule 9 apply in respect of any order against the Government. (2) An application under the proviso to section 31(1) for a direction that a separate certificate is to be issued under that subsection with respect to the costs (if any) ordered to be paid to the applicant, may be made to the Court by summons without notice.
