        IF NOT (`the application is one under the proviso to section 31(1) for a direction that a separate certificate be issued with respect to costs`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 11(2) speaks of "An application under the proviso to section 31(1) for a direction that a separate certificate is to be issued"
        IF document EQUALS Summons AND `the application is made without notice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be made to the Court by summons without notice" gives a permission and says nothing of any other mode

`o 59 r 11(3) the form of the certificate` MEANS "87"

