      `it is in respect of money due or accruing due, or alleged to be due or accruing due, from the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 12(1) the order may be made` MEANS
    IF (NOT (kind EQUALS `o 59 r 12(1) another kind of order`)) AND `it is in respect of money due or accruing due, or alleged to be due or accruing due, from the Government`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be made or have effect in respect of any money due or accruing due, or alleged to be due or accruing due, from the Government"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only the two kinds of order are named, and only in respect of money due from the Government

