    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be made or have effect in respect of any money due or accruing due, or alleged to be due or accruing due, from the Government"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only the two kinds of order are named, and only in respect of money due from the Government

-- (2): the application under section 33(1) "must be made by summons served at least 4 days before the return day on the Government and,
-- unless the Court otherwise orders, on the person to be restrained or that person's solicitor; and ... supported by an affidavit setting
-- out the facts giving rise to it, and in particular identifying the particular debt".
`o 59 r 12(2) the period for serving the summons before the return day` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 4
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

-- src:6966 | (2) Every application to the Court for an order under section 33(1), restraining any person from receiving money payable to that person by the Government and directing payment of the money to the applicant or some other person must be made by summons served at least 4 days before the return day on the Government and, unless the Court otherwise orders, on the person to be restrained or that person’s solicitor; and the application must be supported by an affidavit setting out the facts giving rise to it, and in particular identifying the particular debt from the Government in respect of which it is made.
@ref O 59 r 12(2) (src:6966)
GIVEN `the application is one under section 33(1) restraining a person from receiving money payable to that person by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `Document kind`
      `the summons is served on the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons is served on the person to be restrained or that person's solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the later of the services` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the application is supported by an affidavit setting out the facts giving rise to it and identifying the particular debt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 59 r 12(2) the application is made and served as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is one under section 33(1) restraining a person from receiving money payable to that person by the Government`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 12(2) speaks of "Every application to the Court for an order under section 33(1), restraining any person from receiving money payable to that person by the Government"
        IF `the date of the later of the services` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "served at least 4 days before the return day"
        IF document EQUALS Summons AND `the summons is served on the Government` AND (`the Court otherwise orders` OR `the summons is served on the person to be restrained or that person's solicitor`) AND `the application is supported by an affidavit setting out the facts giving rise to it and identifying the particular debt`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be made by summons served ... and supported by an affidavit"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

